<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Reproducibility</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Data and Code Availability</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All code and pretrained assets are publicly available:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Code:</span> <a href="https://github.com/aviralchawla/metaothello" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://github.com/aviralchawla/metaothello</a></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Models &amp; probes:</span> <a href="https://huggingface.co/aviralchawla/metaothello" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/aviralchawla/metaothello</a></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Training data:</span> <a href="https://huggingface.co/datasets/aviralchawla/metaothello" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://huggingface.co/datasets/aviralchawla/metaothello</a></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The repository includes the MetaOthello game engine, data generation and model training scripts, board probe training and intervention analysis code, and all pretrained checkpoints. See
the repository README for installation and reproduction instructions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Training Details</h3>

<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Architecture.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All models use an 8-layer decoder-only Transformer with 8 attention heads per layer, embedding dimension <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\text{model}}=512" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mtext>model</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>512</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\text{model}}=512</annotation></semantics></math> We use learned positional embeddings with a context window of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=59" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>59</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=59</annotation></semantics></math> tokens. The vocabulary size is 66 (64 board positions plus a skip token and a pad token).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Optimizer.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use AdamW <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Loshchilov and Hutter, 2019</a>)</cite> with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{2}=0.99" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.99</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{2}=0.99</annotation></semantics></math>, and weight decay <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0.01" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0.01</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Learning rate.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a linear warmup over the first 1,000 steps to <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math> over the remaining training.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Batch size.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a batch size of 4096 sequences.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training duration.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Single-game models are trained for 250 epochs on 20M sequences. Mixed-game models are trained for 250 epochs on 40M sequences. Training converges well before 250 epochs; we use this fixed budget for consistency.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Probe Training Details</h3>

<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Architecture.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Linear probes are single-layer linear classifiers mapping from <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{512}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>512</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{512}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> (for mine/yours/empty classification) per board position, yielding 64 independent 3-way classifiers.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Training data.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Probes are trained on 100,000 sequences (sampled independently from model training data) with an 80/20 train/validation split.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Optimizer.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Adam with learning rate <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3\times 10^{-5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3\times 10^{-5}</annotation></semantics></math>, trained for 10 epochs with early stopping based on validation accuracy (patience = 5 epochs).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Game-identity probes.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">These use the same architecture but predict <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(\text{game}\mid s_{&lt;t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>game</mtext><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(\text{game}\mid s_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math> as a binary classification task, trained with cross-entropy loss against the Bayesian ground truth computed from Equation <a href="#A2.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ B.1 Ground Truth Distribution in Mixed Environments ‣ Appendix B Model performance and 𝛼 score ‣ MetaOthello: A Controlled Study of Multiple World Models in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Random Seeds</h3>

<div id="A1.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">All model and probes training a fixed random seed (42) for reproducibility. Due to computational constraints the all models are only trained once.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Model performance and <math id="A2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> score</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Standard metrics such as cross-entropy loss or top-1 accuracy are insufficient for evaluating model performance in the MetaOthello setting. Because the size of the valid move set <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|V(s,g)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|V(s,g)|</annotation></semantics></math> varies significantly depending on the game variant <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> and the game state <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>, the intrinsic entropy of the ground truth distribution fluctuates. A loss of 2.0 nats might represent perfect performance in a high-entropy state (many valid moves) but poor performance in a low-entropy state (forced move).</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To address this, we introduce the <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-score, a normalized metric that measures how much of the reducible uncertainty the model has resolved, relative to a random baseline.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Ground Truth Distribution in Mixed Environments</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In a mixed-game setting, the ground truth distribution over the next token <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, given a history <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{&lt;t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{&lt;t}</annotation></semantics></math>, is a mixture distribution marginalized over the set of possible games <math id="A2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}=\{g_{1},\dots,g_{K}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}=\{g_{1},\dots,g_{K}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">First, we define the likelihood of observing a sequence <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{&lt;t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{&lt;t}</annotation></semantics></math> under a specific game <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>. Assuming the data generation process samples move uniformly from the set of valid moves <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(s_{&lt;k},g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(s_{&lt;k},g)</annotation></semantics></math> at each step <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, the likelihood is the product of the inverse valid move set sizes:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="P(s_{&lt;t}\mid g)=\prod_{k=0}^{t-1}\frac{1}{|V(s_{&lt;k},g)|}\cdot\mathbb{I}[s_{k}\in V(s_{&lt;k},g)]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(s_{&lt;t}\mid g)=\prod_{k=0}^{t-1}\frac{1}{|V(s_{&lt;k},g)|}\cdot\mathbb{I}[s_{k}\in V(s_{&lt;k},g)]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{I}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> is the indicator function, which is <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> if a move is illegal in game <math id="A2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">We define the posterior probability that the current sequence is being generated by game <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> using Bayes’ theorem. Let <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(g)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(g)</annotation></semantics></math> be the prior probability of sampling game <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> (in our mixed datasets, <math id="A2.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(g)=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(g)=0.5</annotation></semantics></math>). The posterior is:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(g\mid s_{&lt;t})=\frac{P(s_{&lt;t}\mid g)P(g)}{\sum_{g^{\prime}\in\mathcal{G}}P(s_{&lt;t}\mid g^{\prime})P(g^{\prime})}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(g\mid s_{&lt;t})=\frac{P(s_{&lt;t}\mid g)P(g)}{\sum_{g^{\prime}\in\mathcal{G}}P(s_{&lt;t}\mid g^{\prime})P(g^{\prime})}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">Substituting the likelihood from Eq. <a href="#A2.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ B.1 Ground Truth Distribution in Mixed Environments ‣ Appendix B Model performance and 𝛼 score ‣ MetaOthello: A Controlled Study of Multiple World Models in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> we obtain the formulation described in the main text: the probability of a game is proportional to the product of the inverse valid move set sizes along the sequence.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p">Finally, the ground truth probability of the next token <math id="A2.SS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is the expectation over the game posteriors:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p9" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{GT}}(x_{t}\mid s_{&lt;t})=\sum_{g\in\mathcal{G}}P(x_{t}\mid s_{&lt;t},g)P(g\mid s_{&lt;t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>GT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{GT}}(x_{t}\mid s_{&lt;t})=\sum_{g\in\mathcal{G}}P(x_{t}\mid s_{&lt;t},g)P(g\mid s_{&lt;t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p10.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(x_{t}\mid s_{&lt;t},g)=|V(s_{&lt;t},g)|^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(x_{t}\mid s_{&lt;t},g)=|V(s_{&lt;t},g)|^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is valid in <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.SS1.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> otherwise.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>The <math id="A2.SS2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-Score Definition</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We seek a metric <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(\theta\mid s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(\theta\mid s)</annotation></semantics></math> that quantifies the model <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>’s proximity to <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{\text{GT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>GT</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{\text{GT}}</annotation></semantics></math>. We define two reference divergences:</p>
<ol id="A2.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model Divergence:</span> <math id="A2.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{GT}}\parallel Q_{\theta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>GT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{GT}}\parallel Q_{\theta})</annotation></semantics></math>, the excess entropy of the model relative to the ground truth.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Random Baseline Divergence:</span> <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{GT}}\parallel U)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>GT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{GT}}\parallel U)</annotation></semantics></math>, the excess entropy of a uniform distribution <math id="A2.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> (random guessing over the vocabulary) relative to the ground truth.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>-score is defined as:</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A2.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(\theta\mid s)=1-\frac{D_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{GT}}\parallel Q_{\theta})}{D_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{GT}}\parallel U)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>GT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>KL</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mtext>GT</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>U</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(\theta\mid s)=1-\frac{D_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{GT}}\parallel Q_{\theta})}{D_{\text{KL}}(P_{\text{GT}}\parallel U)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">This metric has the following desirable properties:</p>
<ul id="A2.I2" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=1</annotation></semantics></math>: The model perfectly matches the ground truth mixture distribution (<math id="A2.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q_{\theta}=P_{\text{GT}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>P</mi><mtext>GT</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q_{\theta}=P_{\text{GT}}</annotation></semantics></math>). This implies the model has perfectly disentangled the ambiguous games or perfectly modeled the superposition.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math>: The model performs equivalent to random guessing over the vocabulary.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&lt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&lt;0</annotation></semantics></math>: The model is being confidently wrong (assigning low probability to valid moves).</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">It is naturally extensible to other comparisons besides the uniform distribution <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>; for instance, in a mixed game setting, we could replace <math id="A2.I2.i4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> with the distribution of next moves according to one of the two games.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I2.i5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I2.i5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I2.i5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Crucially, <math id="A2.I2.i5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> allows us to compare performance across games with vastly different branching factors (e.g., Delflank vs. NoMidFlip) on a unified scale.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F7" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.23164v1/model_accuracy_over_moves_alpha.svg" id="A2.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/248;" width="429" height="248"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A2.F7.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>: </span><span id="A2.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Alpha scores of all models for sequences sampled from each game, shown as a function of move number with 95% intervals.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Probe performance</h2>

<figure id="A3.F8" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.23164v1/board_probe_accuracy_over_moves.svg" id="A3.F8.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:429/374;" width="429" height="374"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F8.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 8</span>: </span><span id="A3.F8.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Accuracies of linear probes trained to detect board states from model activations.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F9" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.23164v1/disagreement_vs_cosine_combined_Classic_NoMidFlip.svg" id="A3.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:234/188;" width="234" height="188"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.23164v1/disagreement_vs_principal_angle_combined_Classic_NoMidFlip.svg" id="A3.F9.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:234/189;" width="234" height="189"></object></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F9.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span id="A3.F9.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(Left) Cosine similarity and (Right) Principal angle (deg.) between Classic and NoMidFlip tile-state representations, plotted against the actual probability that a given tile will have a conflicting state under the two rules.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F10" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2602.23164v1/prob_collapse_NoMidFlip.svg" id="A3.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/168;" width="238" height="168"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F10.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 10</span>: </span><span id="A3.F10.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Change in inferred <math id="A3.F10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(\text{Classic}|s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Classic</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(\text{Classic}|s)</annotation></semantics></math> after playing a move only legal under Classic rules at the end of an ambiguous sequence <math id="A3.F10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>s</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under optimal behavior, the probability of NoMidFlip should collapse to 0 and the probability of Classic to 1; we ask how close the inferred probability gets, compared to its value prior to this move.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A3.F11" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2602.23164v1/tile_state_similarity.png" id="A3.F11.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/571;" width="476" height="571" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F11.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 11</span>: </span><span id="A3.F11.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Cosine similarity of tile-state representations from each layer’s probe for Classic and NoMidFlip (Left) and Classic and DelFlank (Right).</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
